BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (BizMoney Explained frames the signature failure in one line: a business spends $50,000 on a machine that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (works perfectly, sales climb, and three months later it cannot pay its employees [Q4yDbzFte3g @ 00:00:00].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (The same channel traces how the bill outruns the sticker. A $60,000 machine picks up $2,000 in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (transportation, $3,000 in installation, and $1,000 in training; finance $50,000 over five years at 10 percent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (and the payment is roughly $1,062, interest runs about $13,700, and total cash out approaches $80,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (before maintenance, insurance, and repairs [Q4yDbzFte3g @ 00:08:31]. Then demand breaks. A printing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (machine modeled at $2,500 of monthly incremental cash against a $1,500 payment looks fine until weak) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (demand drops the benefit to $900, opening a $600 monthly hole that has to be plugged from reserves or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (other revenue [Q4yDbzFte3g @ 00:13:05]. Joe Camberato's quick test runs the other direction: a $25,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (machine over five years is about $500 a month, so the question is whether it earns more than $500 a month) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (inside the business [H6xXORaU7Jo @ 00:02:53]. The gap between those framings is the whole economics) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (check: Camberato asks if it clears the payment, BizMoney asks if it still clears it in a bad month.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (Personal exposure is the trap nobody prices into the payment. Construction Brothers explain that surety is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (not insurance: the contractor signs an indemnity, and if the surety spends $1 million finishing a job, it comes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (knocking for a payment plan and access to stocks, bonds, and cash accounts [PaYgE9PgaO4 @ 00:03:21].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (Subcontractor default insurance avoids that direct pledge, but the sub still signed a scope of work, so a court) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (can still award damages that land on personal finances, and many big GCs run SDI as a profit center) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (collecting premium from subs and a fee from the owner. BizMoney Explained flags the equipment-side) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (version: personal guarantees that drag the owner's personal finances into a business default, and blanket) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (liens reaching assets beyond the financed machine that restrict future borrowing or refinancing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm ([Q4yDbzFte3g @ 00:19:20]. That cuts against Joe Camberato's pitch that an equipment lease puts the lien) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (on the piece of equipment, not the business [H6xXORaU7Jo @ 00:02:18], and BizMoney's warning is the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (reason to read the collateral clause before taking that pitch at face value. The Banking Podcast adds the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (self-inflicted version: owners who run equipment through personal credit cards max them out, watch the) Tj ET
