BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 621.77 Tm (Ryan Collins says the deal killer he usually does not see coming is a seller who never filed. Lenders must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 606.55 Tm (reconcile the tax returns they receive against IRS transcripts, and more often than people think those returns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 591.32 Tm (were never filed or never recognized by the IRS. That either kills the deal or causes a delay while the seller) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 576.10 Tm (files [8-4I4VOIIqg @ 00:38:11]. Cash-heavy businesses such as restaurants, bars, nail salons, barbers and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 560.87 Tm (tattoo shops are valued only on what appears on the tax return, regardless of the sales report or P&L) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 545.65 Tm ([8-4I4VOIIqg @ 00:10:37]. Add-backs fail when the expense was never expensed or never hit the return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 530.42 Tm (Pairing a cash-basis return with an accrual-basis P&L produces large swings in margins, and Collins will not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.20 Tm (accept that mismatch. He puts a normal timeline at 45 to 60 days, and every gap like this pushes it out. Jeff) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 499.97 Tm (Hildebrandt adds a deadline trap: under SBA guidelines the seller's returns must be received by June 30. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 484.75 Tm (seller on an October extension either produces drafts or waits, because they cannot take the extension and) Tj ET
